TASK-191.3 runtime harness: Settings > Links (Air Traffic Control routes).
Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. It seeds spaces Work, Personal
and Side Project and routes of every kind (URL-only "Domain is work.test" ->
Work, app-only Mail -> Personal, "Contains docs" from Safari -> Work,
"Contains secret" -> Private Window, a broken "Domain is old.test" to a space
that does not exist, added with the store's space check off), the Default
-> Side Project, opens Settings > Links and drives it with real input
(NSApp.postEvent clicks and keys, Detour activated and the Settings window
key first; a pop-up is opened by a posted mouse-down and its item performed
from a .common-mode timer while the menu tracks, then the menu cancelled).
Every step logs the store, the rows as shown and the resolver's decision for
sample links, from the live store (the same call the entry points make).
Steps: New Route (click), Any URL on the draft, back to Domain is, type
news.test + Return, Open in -> Work, edit the first pattern (click, Cmd+A,
type, Return) and deliver https://corp.test/next through
openExternalURLs, match kind Is equal to (refused) / Domain is / Contains,
From app Finder / Any App, reorder (stub NSDraggingInfo through the table's
data source), remove (⊖), Default -> Personal, rename Work elsewhere,
Choose… (the NSOpenPanel sheet captured, cancelled), the blocked-deletion
alert from the sidebar, the Spaces pane "−" and an Undo Add Space, each
answered "Open Links Settings…", a broken Default (step L0), the empty
state, 20+ routes (cap + scroll), then a posted drag (step N). Steps R1-R4
(after the code review): type into a draft and click New Route without
Return; type into a draft and change its Open in pop-up; type and Tab out;
empty a saved route's pattern and move it to another space (both refused)
before the sidebar delete of its saved space. describeRows logs each
warning label's frame against its row and whether the row is highlighted
(read with Mirror from the row view).

