Traps met:
- A posted mouse-down + drags on a row's handle STARTS a real drag session,
  but the session follows the real pointer: in the first run it stayed open
  after the posted mouse-up, swallowed the next posted click (a ⊖) and then
  dropped at wherever the pointer was (moving a route), and later pop-up
  clicks no longer opened their menus; the undo-path alert never showed in
  that run either. The reorder is therefore driven through a stub
  NSDraggingInfo (validateDrop + acceptDrop), and the posted drag runs last
  (step N), where it moved nothing.
- With the screen locked every posted click and menu fails silently (the
  harness falls back to selectItem + sendAction and logs it); runs made
  locked were discarded.

